&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49934902</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:51:27 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Outis – Fight AI spam by sending fake "user unknown" bounce emails</title><link>https://github.com/dtonon/outis</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Outis fights spam generating and sending a fake "user unknown" bounce for an email you received, so the sender believes your address does not exist.&lt;p&gt;Of course this isn't a novel idea, I created a similar program back in 1998–1999 (actually, with a slightly different purpose), but I decided to revive it because it should work quite well with the recent trend of automated emails generated by AI, where the sender might expect a reply; it helps remove your email address from their list.&lt;p&gt;I don't have strong evidence about its effectiveness, but I'm testing it for few weeks and the spam noise seems to be reduced; I don't receive similar or followup emails any more.&lt;p&gt;Any idea on how to improve it? :)&lt;/p&gt;
